	(text "For a read of N drive words:\n1. With both strobes inactive, configure IODIRA = IODIRB = 0xFF. Finish that configuration transaction with CS high.\n2. Select the drive register.\n   Set the drive's address and chip-select lines while strobes remain inactive. \n   These are separate from the expander's CS. For a data-register burst, establish the appropriate ATAPI data-in phase and byte count first.\n3. Select read mode.\n   Keep ~{ATAPI_CS} = HIGH and ~{ATAPI_BURST} = HIGH; set ATAPI_WRITE = LOW. U6B is now held reset. Ensure U6A's previous pulse has expired (adjust R1/C1 during assembly if not).\n4. Assert the initial drive read.\n   Lower ~{ATAPI_CS}. With U6A.Q low, this immediately asserts ~{DIOR}. Leave ~{BURST} HIGH.\n5. Allow data to settle.\n   Account for the drive's data-valid delay, any buffering, and the expander's input propagation. Handle IORDY if required by the drive/mode.\n6. Send the SPI header: 0x41, 0x12. Keep ~{ATAPI_CS} low afterward. The drive continues presenting its first word.\n7. Enable payload counting.\n   Stop SCK low, lower ~{ATAPI_BURST}, and satisfy the counter's reset-recovery time before starting payload clocks.\n8. Receive exactly 2N − 1 16-bit SPI words, that is 4N − 2 received bytes. Keep ~{ATAPI_CS} low throughout.\n   What happens:\n   - 1-16	Receive drive word 1; keep it\n   - After clock 16	Q4 rises; U6A drives DIOR_n HIGH, ending that read\n   - During 17-32	U6A's pulse expires; DIOR_n goes LOW for the next read; discard this SPI word\n   - 33-48	Receive drive word 2; keep it\n   …	Repeat\n9. Raise ~{ATAPI_CS} promptly after the final payload clock.\n   Use hardware-timed CS release with verified timing. \n   CS must inhibit the read path before U6A's final recovery pulse expires; otherwise another drive read begins. \n   Do not wait for a scheduled task or insert a microsecond/millisecond delay here.\n10. Then raise ~{ATAPI_BURST}.\n    This resets the counter. Preserve drive address/chip-select hold time before deselecting the drive.\n11. Keep received word indices 0, 2, 4… (bytes 0-1, 4-5, ...)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.686 212.598 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "528a411b-ab90-4f29-87ea-ea1bb1380fa3")
	)
	(text "Power"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 394.97 183.642 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a0fc45cd-1a9e-491c-9afb-5ba8aa5b4d74")
	)
	(text "For a write of N drive words, use this sequence.\n1. With ~{ATAPI_CS} = HIGH, ~{ATAPI_BURST} = HIGH, set ATAPI_WRITE = HIGH. \n   Configure IODIRA = IODIRB = 0x00 while the drive is not driving the data bus.\n2. Select the drive register and establish readiness.\n3. Lower ~{ATAPI_CS}, keeping ~{ATAPI_BURST} HIGH.\n   ATAPI_WRITE = HIGH inhibits reads; ~{ATAPI_BURST} = HIGH inhibits writes.\n4. Send the SPI header: 0x40, 0x12. \n   The counter ignores these 16 clocks because reset remains asserted. Keep CS low afterward.\n5. Ensure U6B's startup pulse has expired by a software delay.\n   Changing ATAPI_WRITE from LOW to HIGH can trigger U6B through reset release. \n   ~{ATAPI_BURST} masks that pulse, but it must finish before ~{ATAPI_BURST} is lowered.\n6. Stop SCK low and lower ~{ATAPI_BURST}.\n7. Transmit exactly 2N payload bytes, low byte first per word.\n   After every 16 payload clocks, Q3 falls and U6B generates a LOW pulse on ~{DIOW}. Its rising edge completes the write.\n8. Raise ~{ATAPI_CS} after the last payload clock.\n9. Wait for the final write to complete.\n   Keep ATAPI_WRITE HIGH, ~{ATAPI_BURST} LOW, the output data unchanged, and the drive selected throughout this interval.\n10. Raise ~{ATAPI_BURST}, then finish deselecting the drive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.654 261.366 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ad6ce388-0bce-43d8-ba19-76cbd21e4ba3")
	)
	(text "Cursed SPI to IDE clock division"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.594 184.912 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "cf09a371-9de3-49cc-9fc6-c1ddb758013e")
	)
	(text "Initialize the interface as follows.\n1. Establish ~{ATAPI_CS} = HIGH, ~{ATAPI_BURST} = HIGH, ATAPI_WRITE = HIGH. Both drive strobes are inhibited.\n2. Configure SPI for 5 MHz, mode 0, MSB first.\n3. Configure the MCP23S17 with BANK = 0, SEQOP = 1; disable input polarity inversion.\n4. Give A0-A2 definite levels. The examples below assume address zero, giving SPI opcodes 0x40 for writes and 0x41 for reads.\n5. Ensure any previous one-shot pulses have finished before beginning an operation.\nWith that configuration, successive accesses starting at GPIOA, address 0x12, alternate between A and B."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.622 201.676 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "efa3fbad-6195-46df-b9f5-c589a07950bd")
	)
